==Comparison==
Oathplate armour is ideal against enemies with high Defence that are susceptible to slash attacks, such as [[Vardorvis]], [[Duke Sucellus]], [[Verzik Vitur]], and even Yama himself. In these situations, the slash accuracy bonus provided by Oathplate meaningfully improves hit chance, which can make up for the lower strength bonus than [[Torva armour]]. Against enemies that are equally weak to all melee types with high Defence, such as the [[Great Olm]], Oathplate is marginally better compared to [[Bandos armour]] and [[Torva armour]]. Against enemies that are equally weak to all melee but with very low Defence, Torva armour can outperform Oathplate.

Compared to Torva armour, Oathplate gains offensive slash bonus, has lower strength bonus, and lacks any prayer bonus. The other bonuses are mixed, Oathplate has stronger slash and magic defence, but less stab, crush, and ranged defence. It also penalises magic attack slightly less than Torva, and penalises ranged attack more.

The armour's strength bonus is on par with [[Bandos armour]] and a [[Neitiznot faceguard]]. Considering the full "set" (of [[bandos chestplate]], [[bandos tassets]] and faceguard), Oathplate has slightly higher stab and crush defence, significantly higher slash defence, slightly less ranged and magic defence and lacks any prayer bonus. Given the similar defence capabilities, Oathplate is far superior when using slash weapons, due to the slash accuracy. Defensively, is an upgrade in encounters against melee opponents where prayers cannot completely block damage.

[[Inquisitor's armour]] is only better when using crush attacks. Oathplate does not have a passive effect, but is more flexible than gear which requires multiple pieces to make use of a set effect. The Inquisitor’s has significantly worse defence bonuses compared to Oathplate.

==Radiant oathplate==
Oathplate armour can be cosmetically upgraded to [[radiant oathplate armour]] using a [[purifying sigil]]. This works similarly to the [[Ancient blood ornament kit]], used to create [[sanguine torva armour]]. This sigil requires the player to defeat Yama in five distinct scenarios: the [[Contract of Bloodied Blows]], [[Contract of Divine Severance]], [[Contract of Forfeit Breath]], [[Contract of Glyphic Attenuation]], and [[Contract of Sensory Clouding]].

Alongside the sigil, 2,500 [[aether rune]]s are required to convert each piece for a total of 7,500 for the entire set.

